{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>Take, please, my blessing.</b> The gift. And similarly: עֲשׂוּ אִתִּי בְרָכָה (2 Kings 18:31); הָשִׁיבוּ לִי מִנְחָה; and similarly: קַח נָא בְרָכָה מֵאֵת עַבְדֶּךָ (2 Kings 5:15). And they call the gift that a man sends for his favor a 'blessing,' because he sends from that with which HaShem has blessed him, in the manner of: אֲשֶׁר בֵּרַכְךָ ה' אֱלֹהֶיךָ תִּתֶּן לוֹ (Deuteronomy 15:14), as he said above (Genesis 32:14): מִן הַבָּא בְיָדוֹ. And the gift that they gave to the king is called by a known term: מַס (tribute)."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:21:58.122856297Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}